      source:{ cite:'RPAPL 731(1), (4); 701(1); 711', quote:'RPAPL 731(1): The special proceeding prescribed by this article shall be commenced by petition and a notice of petition. A notice of petition may be issued only by an attorney, judge or the clerk of the court; it may not be issued by a party prosecuting the proceeding in person.\n\nRPAPL 731(4): In an action premised on a tenant defaulting in the payment of rent, payment to the landlord of the full amount of rent due, when such payment is made at any time prior to the hearing on the petition, shall be accepted by the landlord and renders moot the grounds on which the special proceeding was commenced.',
        from:S9_FROM, context:'How a landlord-tenant summary proceeding starts and who may issue the notice of petition.', url:'https://www.nysenate.gov/legislation/laws/RPA/731' },
      hook:'A-J-C: Attorney, Judge, Clerk. Never the landlord on his own.',
